PASS: Real CWE-93 field injection. GHSA-gcq2-9pq2-cxqm and CVE-2026-55603 (cveMetadata.state=PUBLISHED at https://cveawg.mitre.org/api/cve/CVE-2026-55603; GitHub withdrawn_at is null) document that fixRequestBody rebuilds an outgoing multipart/form-data body by interpolating req.body keys/values into boundary-delimited parts without neutralizing CR/LF. Source is attacker-controlled body fields after a non-multipart parser; sink is handlerFormDataBodyData writing `--${boundary}
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="${key}"

${value}
` onto proxyReq. JSON/urlencoded siblings use JSON.stringify/querystring.stringify and do not share this sink. Preconditions match the advisory (non-multipart in, multipart out, fixRequestBody). The GHSA PoC is the same interpolation that exists at a12a59df42507659e536ce60c04ee7f97dd5aad5, 5d9f46f72010c3512a859179ec43b54f521e7fa1, v3.0.4, v3.0.6, v4.0.0, and v4.1.0.
